
# `location` is the universal whereabouts belief label: {X location Y} reads
# "X is/was at place Y" for both props (the building/space a prop sits in) and
# people (the dated where-were-you memory). The explicit (tar ?) keeps the state
# target UNCONSTRAINED - a location may be a building, a room/space, an exterior
# address-space, or a mental org object. @excl: a subject is in exactly ONE place
# at a time, so minting a new whereabouts ENDS the prior one (closing its
# interval) - without this an NPC accumulates many never-ending {X location Y}
# beliefs and the comings-and-goings timeline is unreadable. (theme frequent)
# routes ended whereabouts episodes through the sleep-time themed fuse: routine
# comings-and-goings compress into the semantic gist while flashbulb-buffed
# whereabouts (intensity-stamped by a co-occurring high-emotion event) survive
# as the peak exemplar - the detective-relevant "I remember where I was".
location (+ obs) (state) (tar ? @excl) (theme frequent) (location)

# `building` used as a belief label is spatial CONTAINMENT: {<space> building
# <building>} = the space is enclosed by that building (the reverse of the
# {<building> room <space>} skeleton link). The spatial index maps space ->
# building off it. `building` is also a noun kind (Objects.mon); this explicit
# (state) entry overrides the auto-generated noun-state placeholder in place to
# attach the (containment) flag - the noun kind is untouched. Ownership was split
# off to `owns_building` (Concepts.mon) so this label carries only the spatial sense.
building (state) (tar building @excl) (building)

# `frequent` is location's semantic-summary label: the themed fuse folds a
# subject's ended {X location <place>} episodes into an ongoing
# {X frequent <place>} gist. It MUST be a different label from `location`
# (episodic vs semantic must never share a label): location is @excl, and a
# same-label summary would overlap the retained first/last/peak episodes and
# trip the exclusivity validator. Non-excl on purpose - a subject frequents
# many places over overlapping spans. Subject unconstrained (props accumulate
# whereabouts episodes too).
frequent (tar ?)

# env_point: nav waypoints / spawnpoints (the env_point.arc archetype). Renamed
# from the old `location` archetype/kind so the `location` name is reserved for
# the whereabouts belief-label above and the space-as-location model (exterior
# spaces are `space` entities, not env_points). Dormant in hsim - GrymEngine
# runtime nav/spawn instantiates these.
env_point (+ obs)
    waypoint
    spawnpoint
